+# Garage revised draft and typography correction
+
+GRD01–GRD05, 15 November 2026. The owner's new reference supersedes the previous subtle text overlay. The later font feedback also supersedes the draft's synthetic italic treatment.
+
+The Garage now has a bordered left-hand profile with a single car title, character subtitle, five-segment Acceleration/Handling/Top speed comparisons, dividers and short description. All profile typography uses the same upright Barlow display/body faces as the rest of the game. The temporary transform-based italics were removed after the owner identified distorted letters.
+
+The selected car occupies more of the showroom, with separate breathing room for the Forklift mast and Volt/Hover silhouettes. The existing showroom's camera callback provides this selection-only composition; `car_showroom.gd` remains byte-exact to the task-start source. Workshop focus, rotation, zoom, saved paint, kits and wear retain their original ownership. The drag hint sits at the lower right. Rounded whole-pixel carousel heights prevent focus from scrolling a fully visible card out from under a subsequent touch.
+
+Four car cards fit the standard layout; smaller windows expose three and retain horizontal browsing. New 512×288 transparent stock portraits render the actual production cars with native finishes and Garage lighting, without the earlier miniature platforms. Saved custom paint, kits and visible wear continue through the existing appearance-specific preview path. The gold border follows the browsed car immediately; the checkmark/Selected badge identifies the equipped car. This resolves the draft's mismatch between a Super Rally profile and selected Rally card without mislabeling the equipped vehicle.
+
+The footer uses compact right-aligned Select vehicle and outlined Test drive actions. The Garage header uses underline navigation and an account coin balance beside the retained car/profile controls. Guests show an unavailable balance, without a fabricated 3,500 coins. Leaving Garage restores the ordinary header; returning retains the Garage page and showroom.
+
+Comparison scales are presentation only. Acceleration uses the qualified clean unboosted 0–60 km/h time, with `round(4 / seconds)` clamped to five segments. Top speed uses `round(km/h / 60)`, also clamped; five segments correspond to 300 km/h. Handling is an authored ease-of-control comparison: Rally 4, Kart 5, Forklift 2, Volt 3, Hover 1 and Super Rally 4. These values describe different driving characters and do not modify a tune or claim physical grip measurements. Exact configured top speed and measured acceleration are available in hover tooltips; tooltip routing preserves drag-through input. Super Rally matches the draft's 4/4/3 bars.
+
+Runtime changes: `game/ui/garage_car_stats.gd`, `garage_page.gd`, `garage_header.gd`, `garage_selection_camera.gd`, `garage_selection_pictures.gd`, `garage_cached_thumbnail.gd`, and three header-composition lines in `game/core/app.gd`. Supporting changes: the native portrait producer and renderer under `game/tests/`, the reference regression plus presentation-specific assertions in the existing stats suite, `scripts/check_garage_selection_pictures.py`, a narrow Android preflight hook/raw-image inclusion, portrait provenance, 19 directly authored phrases across twelve catalogues/source template, and narrow identity exclusions for selection-only helpers/derived pictures. Unknown vehicle inputs and room reflections remain shared dependencies. Existing concurrent App, Garage, vehicle and index changes were preserved.
+
+The portrait producer renders privately, verifies 25,150 consumed inputs, then publishes six PNGs and a manifest last. Consumers verify source revisions, per-image hashes and dimensions; export additionally verifies producer/recipe hashes. Derived portraits are excluded from their own source identity. No old prepared scene or catalogue manifest was restamped to make it appear current. Broader prepared-car/workshop/catalogue readiness is outside this UI qualification.
+
+Actual commands used the pinned Godot 4.7.2 and isolated local records, with an empty backend URL:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/check_model_refinement_parse.gd
+python scripts/run_garage_car_stats.py gl_compatibility-reference-portraits res://tests/bake_garage_selection_portraits.gd --direct
+python scripts/check_garage_selection_pictures.py
+python scripts/run_garage_car_stats.py headless-reference-header res://tests/test_garage_reference.gd --direct
+python scripts/run_garage_car_stats.py headless-reference-final-language res://tests/test_garage_reference.gd --direct
+python scripts/run_garage_car_stats.py gl_compatibility-reference-final res://tests/test_garage_reference.gd --direct
+python scripts/run_garage_car_stats.py mobile-reference-final res://tests/test_garage_reference.gd --direct
+python scripts/run_garage_car_stats.py selection-reference-final res://tests/test_garage_selection_feedback.gd --direct
+```
+
+Final reference suite: **881/0 headless and 893/0 in each desktop renderer**. It covers six cars, four window sizes, eleven translated language choices, exact measured/configured tooltips, rating distinctions, complete default-car silhouettes, uncropped card footers, equipped badges, stock-portrait resolution/alpha, saved-state preservation, real mouse/touch rotation, balances and header navigation round trips. A final tooltip-only locale notification also passes **4/0** live language changes and a clean **881/0** headless repeat; its command and temporary probe are recorded in `reference-live-language.json`. Existing selection feedback passes **20/0 headless and 23/0 native Compatibility**, including drawn feedback before construction. Production parsing passes **576/0**. All six portraits and their stable-source manifest validate; seven isolated stale/corrupt-asset controls reject bad inputs and preserve accepted files. Targeted translation validation passes **228/0**. Ten focused routing controls retain shared model/lighting dependencies while excluding selection UI/output. Python compilation and scoped whitespace checks pass.
+
+The Compatibility run exits zero but retains the known two-object/one-resource shutdown diagnostic. The final Mobile and headless reference runs exit cleanly. Earlier Mobile stalls remain historical evidence; this task does not identify or claim to fix their cause. Earlier layout/typography/portrait iterations, a temporary camera-clear teardown error, two conservative silhouette findings and a fractional-height touch regression were corrected without weakening the corresponding assertions. The existing broad PowerShell identity fixture still stops on its missing checkpoint `godot-version.txt` dependency; its result is not claimed as passed. Focused routing checks run separately. An initial shell-quoting attempt and execution-policy rejection were corrected before those checks were accepted.
+
+Current views: [standard Garage](evidence/garage-car-stats-2026-11-14/gl_compatibility-reference-final/super_rally-1280.png), [compact Garage](evidence/garage-car-stats-2026-11-14/gl_compatibility-reference-final/super_rally-960.png), [Forklift](evidence/garage-car-stats-2026-11-14/gl_compatibility-reference-final/forklift-1280.png), and [desktop Mobile](evidence/garage-car-stats-2026-11-14/mobile-reference-final/super_rally-1280.png). Logs, command receipts, source/asset controls and the scoped `reference-checkpoint.json` are in the same evidence directory. The historical directory name follows the original stats task; this revision is dated 15 November.
+
+No physical-device test, APK/export, backend operation, deployment, owner-save change, owner-process restart or main-index staging was performed. The existing vehicle geometry, handling and canonical simulation were not authored by this task. Owner appearance and phone qualification remain. Standard build retention was applied; recent/protected output remains above its target.
